    {
      "id": "32bbb68d-cfba-4596-8307-3b60d51c404e",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-15T11:31:36.000Z",
      "title": "Consensus EPS estimates fall by 12%",
      "body": "The consensus outlook for earnings per share (EPS) in fiscal year 2027 has deteriorated. 2027 revenue forecast decreased from ₹106.0b to ₹103.4b. EPS estimate also fell from ₹21.45 per share to ₹18.92 per share. Net income forecast to grow 12% next year vs 41% growth forecast for Real Estate industry in India. Consensus price target broadly unchanged at ₹829. Share price fell 6.8% to ₹567 over the past week.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "96e8f1f1-90ae-4be3-a9b6-4485749a9e64",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-14T12:09:20.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with expectations, revenues disappoint",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹17.83 (up from ₹17.65 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹98.2b (up 23% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹44.1b (up 1.1% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 45% (down from 55% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 9.8%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 16% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 22% growth forecast for the Real Estate industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 29% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 8% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
